Project: Kubernetes. Upgrade: 1.23 -> 1.29. Release of these items: 1.24.
Source: Kubernetes v1.24.0 CHANGELOG.

Label every item:
- risk = the change could break an application or deployment, require migration work, or create operational risk for SOME user upgrading across this release (removed or renamed APIs/settings/flags, changed defaults, behavior changes, raised minimum versions of runtimes/databases/dependencies, data or schema migration, required config changes, deprecated-and-removed features).
- context = accurate and useful but needs no user action at this release: explicitly "no user action required", a deprecation that still works (warning only), a purely additive new feature or option, documentation pointers.
- noise = credits, install/download commands, pure bug fixes that cannot change correct behavior, marketing text, headings with no content.

Return one label per item_id with a one-sentence reason grounded in the item text.

Items (JSON lines):
{"item_id": "ca6e42de0b7f", "section": "v1.24.0 / Changes by Kind / Deprecation", "text": "The cluster addon for dashboard was removed. To install dashboard, see here."}
{"item_id": "956b434065df", "section": "v1.24.0 / Changes by Kind / Deprecation", "text": "The in-tree Azure plugin has been deprecated. The Azure kubelogin plugin serves as an out-of-tree replacement via the kubectl/client-go credential plugin mechanism. Users will now see a warning in the logs regarding this deprecation."}
{"item_id": "09e322a484d2", "section": "v1.24.0 / Changes by Kind / Deprecation", "text": "The insecure address flags --address and --port in kube-controller-manager have had no effect since v1.20 and are removed in v1.24."}
{"item_id": "56b3c7be5133", "section": "v1.24.0 / Changes by Kind / Deprecation", "text": "The metadata.clusterName field is deprecated. This field has always been unwritable and always blank, but its presence is confusing, so we will remove it next release. Out of an abundance of caution, this release we have merely changed the name in the go struct to ensure any accidental client uses are found before complete removal."}
{"item_id": "8c22fbfa856c", "section": "v1.24.0 / Changes by Kind / Deprecation", "text": "VSphere releases less than 7.0u2 are deprecated as of v1.24. Please consider upgrading vSphere to 7.0u2 or above. vSphere CSI Driver requires minimum vSphere 7.0u2. General Support for vSphere 6.7 will end on October 15, 2022. vSphere 6.7 Update 3 is deprecated in Kubernetes v1.24. Customers are recommended to upgrade vSphere (both ESXi and vCenter) to 7.0u2 or above. vSphere CSI Driver 2.2.3 and higher supports CSI Migration. Support for these deprecations will be available till October 15, 2022."}
